;; Glasswood's thin ice with room to jump: twelve cells of it under five rows
;; of air. A jump from the bank lands a few cells onto the ice, and the far
;; bank is still more running than a second on the ice allows, so to the
;; checker it is unreachable. (In the game a player who hops again on each
;; landing resets the count and can cross: the checker never chains hops
;; without a rest, which is the safe direction, and thin ice is no barrier.)
;; A regression case: with the crack switched off it stays unreachable
;; today (sabotage S5b: no searched pattern stays on the ice long enough to
;; crack, since walks end at WALK-MAX = BRITTLE-TICKS and a landing ends a
;; trajectory). It goes red if a pattern is added that runs on after landing
;; AND the crack is lost.
(fixture
  name: "thin ice, twelve cells under open air: unreachable to the checker"
  expect: unreachable
  why: "the checker never rests on thin ice or chains hops without a rest"
  start: (3 7)
  target: ((21 7))
  brittle: ((6 8) (7 8) (8 8) (9 8) (10 8) (11 8) (12 8) (13 8) (14 8) (15 8) (16 8) (17 8))
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "#########################"
   "#########################"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "#########################"
   "######~~~~~~~~~~~~#######"
   "#########################"))
